+
+// Waits (at most ~500 ms) until the peer has acknowledged everything sent,
+// before the next part: then nothing is in flight or queued, and the next
+// part leaves as its own packet at once - with a TTL-1 part right behind
+// an OOB one, the kernel held it back until after the TTL was restored
